{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_14c2ec4ca1804a02c6b60d141348d71d53b2211492427c3d4c2d9c61ba774e2b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=evaluation","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b8ad3fa91f67fcfb04a451c21bcfabe78ed202e59ea82327cf4bd4e4e81092ba","slc_b94008e1473b260c399f4f0f6fdcd3dba53126e6b9539b85bbb24c2738c081b8"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"The architecture claims capability-tier floors (e.g. 7B for single-file edits, hosted frontier for refactors) are 'measured empirically', suggesting some agent-performance evaluation was done, though no eval harness appears in the evidence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_151c0f049be0b8941c038e6e50f43ceb47df0a47305ac940b31f69d338b59b8f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14459c198b2999d548c1488c33daddc0ba1384a26b9e2610440fea3b288844ee","slc_941a2acba3d3c25a716b93f36155f3e6572aedd9641bce30a089f880c3df79c7"],"source_ids":["src_c43ba3092cf857cbbfa8d6abc1d57568","src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Forge auto-detects local providers (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp) on default ports; cloud providers (Anthropic, OpenAI-compatible, etc.) are opt-in rather than required.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d0999541735061d979772aff1d713bc60892e8ef85c26e803effada0d9f7b87","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ce79596ed5350dd4ef099edf5b5d333a74532624267dd665fd9990d49f963433"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Four memory tiers are documented: hot (per-task, cleared on completion), warm (SQLite recent-task metadata), cold (lazy file/grep/AST index), and learning (patterns with confidence, read by the planner).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3c84fa73a87579d4dd5dce64b3e027d783f59cadc6e1cefd8f63a0e78e4d5371","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03af3792438a0b02d11f9eba5ad77f17f033d60bb4c88167f8ac57161d1a0ff9","slc_3f2c32600ab19567cc28632242ed2f944c994c7b0f8724c7c4c42bbb23531dc4"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"The agentic loop flows classify → plan → user approval → DAG execution with a validation gate, bounded retries, and a reviewer step before completion.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4af778d0d79f9ab775256ce8fb6f28a4883fe8039274d2e6cf176c2755d6bcc3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14459c198b2999d548c1488c33daddc0ba1384a26b9e2610440fea3b288844ee","slc_3e48522f344d60db9e582fcfb19716abbad60dc0860c13853b407f11b0629f47"],"source_ids":["src_c43ba3092cf857cbbfa8d6abc1d57568","src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Modes carry enforceable budgets: e.g. fast allows 2 executor turns and 0 validation retries, heavy 8 turns and 2 retries, plan and audit disallow mutations.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_61dc062fdff850671fd58e448e4708fe1b13c2c9ea4f35e424b1defd78eb599d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5176f1e0148797d24bd6a0b8eefebd5b03143b911a9cdc7db83f5967738d6c38","slc_7a5c0479109a4dcc91b173e5b1bfac140d6e52c09522e92f6329ee1d2ae4c7e7","slc_dbbfb3269ba24eb0368bc51b2303d7babce9161130e2f4039e70bed5652ed476"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Tasks move through a state machine (draft, planned, approved, scheduled, running, verifying, completed/failed/blocked/cancelled); illegal transitions throw state_invalid and terminal states re-enter only via forge resume.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_65d310024b1462ebaa0c8110e25ee99a934ecd857d5058cd6bae4fe2f1448c16","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27fce5e64783515e9e6b8b392e7c9daeb11787dc70847cf23224263c1caca91c","slc_5a656b57c19376f6504717764d48b6accf388a360f0db61f37448803c803aa8a"],"source_ids":["src_c43ba3092cf857cbbfa8d6abc1d57568"],"text":"Forge is described as a local-first, plan-first, multi-agent, programmable software-engineering runtime where users pick and host the model and approve actions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7266234cbaba90fccf6c19877c2bc9a0540a89d2f0a3fa20244a275b3068f12e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2fbe5db2125d76579089efda39e0fc4db17a961fb55275eb3cf7899d7c035fe7","slc_617d733c0b98d4900527f266b5891548567f9ad204f4863f7cde030bd907be7c"],"source_ids":["src_c43ba3092cf857cbbfa8d6abc1d57568"],"text":"The runtime has 13 npm dependencies with zero optional, including @modelcontextprotocol/sdk, better-sqlite3, commander, undici, ws, yaml, and zod; Node.js >= 20 is required via package.json engines.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7556f6bccf835d13668ec07db1e1e09c5440f9429bf0b49c989dc47e6d349ee4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_950e22456115201c5c81d5f6d697ae26d920dae55fb07450d4d95b035a5a6b28"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Filesystem access is realpath-resolved and confined to projectRoot plus whitelisted extra roots, with always-forbidden targets like /etc/passwd and SSH keys; grants persist in a SQLite permission_grants table.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7bc3fedf368b02481be35a73a2ba9a73e56e0d47d6ccbb00ec83130d17f0038c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5732dd0fa46aa4497c8af3f9de95acf7728ebb24a9b78034e4a5b813212ced98","slc_950e22456115201c5c81d5f6d697ae26d920dae55fb07450d4d95b035a5a6b28","slc_9de15a7233997ae04ed6a3daf288317605cbcf89d549e5a38bfacf8c6adec3e1"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"Every tool invocation is risk-classified; low-risk reads auto-allow, medium/high risk prompts the user, sandbox violations hard-block, and critical shell commands are blocked regardless of preferences.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b238ccaeb9ece091962f41c9909581f12b83ec25306cad19c1ad3619138d51d8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"hoangsonww/forge-agentic-coding-cli@50e173d93806 snapshot 67f90918cac0237a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e3c7156a95ca20ecc92638b710c1877540996caf652217276bcce842cb4bf743"],"source_ids":["src_c986852811ef5211a8516914c424402b"],"text":"The MCP server exposes read-only tools (forge_status, forge_plan, forge_get_task, forge_list_tasks) by default; forge_run and forge_cancel_task require opt-in via --allow-execute or FORGE_MCP_ALLOW_EXECUTE=true.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8911ecc87f084f3b85559f1f914e816c"}
